ionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:6fa218b9dd33f49baf07d56b"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C and D are both incorrect as written.","reason":"C is false because area scales by four when a circle radius doubles. D is also false for a zero numerator: a/(b) and (a/2)/(2b) are both zero when a=0,b!=0. The statement says the quotient changes without excluding zero.","status":"confirmed_ambiguous"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_009"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":["For a zero-valued fraction, D is also incorrect as written. C is unique under an implicit nonzero-fraction convention."],"questionId":"1951_AMC_12_Q10","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p089","cnm_p148","cnm_017","cnm_009"],"id":"1951_AMC_12_Q10_m1","label":"Check the formulas and the zero case","methodDirectNodeIds":{"1951_AMC_12_Q10_m1":["cnm_p192","cnm_071"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p192","cnm_071","cnm_p089","cnm_p148","cnm_017","cnm_009"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:6fa218b9dd33f49baf07d56b"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D. 11","reason":"The inequality is (n²)^100<125^100, equivalent to n²<125. Since 11²=121<125<144=12², the largest integer n is 11.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_009"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1984_AMC_12_Q05","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_019","cnm_074","cnm_009"],"id":"1984_AMC_12_Q05_m1","label":"Reduce the large powers","methodDirectNodeIds":{"1984_AMC_12_Q05_m1":["cnm_h020","cnm_143","cnm_079"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h020","cnm_143","cnm_079","cnm_019","cnm_074","cnm_009"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:6fa218b9dd33f49baf07d56b"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B: 6","reason":"Write the list as a,b,8,d,e. Its sum is 60 and e=a+18. The case d=8 has sum at most 58, so d>8 and the repeated mode requires b=8. Then d=26−2a, and d≤e with 1≤a≤8 gives a=3,...,8. The six possible d values are 20,18,16,14,12,10.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_009"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1995_AMC_12_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_009","cnm_040"],"id":"1995_AMC_12_Q25_m1","label":"Sort and bound the list","methodDirectNodeIds":{"1995_AMC_12_Q25_m1":["cnm_211","cnm_213","cnm_215","math:integer-diophantine-equations"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_211","cnm_213","cnm_215","math:integer-diophantine-equations","cnm_009","cnm_040"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:6fa218b9dd33f49baf07d56b"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 14","reason":"Write the sorted values as x1≤...≤x8=L. Their sum is 64, x4+x5=16, x5≥8, and x1=L-8. Consequently 64≥3(L-8)+16+16+L=4L+8, so L≤14. The collection {6,6,6,8,8,8,8,14} attains 14 and has mean, median, unique mode, and range all equal to 8.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_009"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2002_AMC_12A_Q15","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_009","cnm_096"],"id":"ordered-bound-and-construction","label":"Bound the total and attain the bound","methodDirectNodeIds":{"ordered-bound-and-construction":["math:extremal-principle","cnm_211","cnm_213","cnm_215"]},"nodeIds":["math:extremal-principle","cnm_211","cnm_213","cnm_215","cnm_009","cnm_096"]}]}],"canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_009"],"label":"有理数的大小比较","layer":"CN","meaning":"Practice covers aligned canonical concepts, with no claim of complete standard coverage or mastery.","nextOffset":null,"sourceNode":{"criteria":["会用数轴比较大小","会比较两个负数的大小"],"description":"利用数轴（右边的数大）和绝对值（负数绝对值大的反而小）比较有理数大小。","id":"cnm_009","label":"有理数的大小比较","original":{"chapter":"七上 第一章 有理数 1.2.5","description":"利用数轴（右边的数大）和绝对值（负数绝对值大的反而小）比较有理数大小。","domain":"数与代数","external":false,"grade":7,"id":"cnm_009","mastery_criteria":["会用数轴